=== IO ===
+ Input and Output of files

== File Classes ==
+ Miscellaneous classes to handle a file
- Not optimized to big files (low level), isn't made for performance

= File =
+ Create, delete and access to several properties of a file

= FileWriter =
+ Write on a file (receives the file reference in constructor)

= FileReader =
+ Read a file (receives the file reference in constructor)

== Buffered classes ==
+ More performance (working with data and memory)
+ A buffer is an array in RAM memory (generally a char[])
+ The data stay temporarily in this buffer at RAM memory
+ When the buffer reaches the maximum of capacity (or was flushed), the data will be read or wrote on file (will try to use the smallest number of readings)

= BufferedWriter =
+ Receives a FileWriter
+ You can pass the size of the buffer

= BufferedReader =
+ Receives a FileReader